  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Debugging\n\n- The package's DLLs carry their PDBs, with Source Link (#514, closes #513). Imposter.CodeGenerator.dll and Imposter.Abstractions.dll used to ship without symbols, so a debugger couldn't step into Imposter's runtime types or the generator. Both now embed their PDB, which points to the exact commit on GitHub through Source Link and embeds the sources git doesn't track. Imposter.Abstractions now also builds with deterministic source paths, as the generator already did, and a build from the same commit reproduces both DLLs byte for byte. The package grows from about 338 KB to 580 KB per Roslyn version.\n\nHousekeeping\n\n- Runtime property helpers renamed (#499, closes #480). PropertyGetter<T>.EnableBaseImplementation is now UseBaseImplementation, matching the setter and the fluent setup API, and PropertySetter<T>.SetForInit is now RecordAndShouldCallBase. These members exist for generated code, which this release regenerates to match; behaviour is unchanged.\n- Documentation fixes in Imposter.Abstractions (#490, #493): wrong XML docs and comments in the runtime types, the generator and the argument matchers are corrected.\n- Generator cleanups with byte-identical output (#485, #486, #488, #489, #491, #492, #495–#498, #500, #501, #503–#508, #510–#512): duplicated builders, metadata and literals are consolidated, unused helpers removed, and member names read from the metadata that declares them.\n- The C# sources are normalized to UTF-8 with a BOM (#494), and a concurrency test's barrier has a timeout (#487).\n- Releases publish to nuget.org through trusted publishing instead of a stored API key (#516, closes #515). The expired key had stopped 1.0.11 from reaching NuGet, so this release carries its changes.",
